  "hindi": "त्रयी में धर्म और अधर्म, वार्ता में अर्थ और अनर्थ, दण्डनीति में नय और अनय, इनके बल और दुर्बलता को हेतुओं से जाँचती हुई लोक का उपकार करती है, व्यसन और अभ्युदय में बुद्धि को स्थापित करती है, और प्रज्ञा, वाक्य, क्रिया की निपुणता करती है।",
  "english": "Examining by reasons dharma and unrighteousness in the triple Veda, gain and loss in economic activity, good policy and bad policy in the policy of punishment, and the strength and weakness of these, [it] benefits the world, establishes the mind in calamity and in prosperity, and brings about proficiency in insight, speech and action.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The subject (feminine, Ānvīkṣikī of unit 10) is not named; English supplies '[it]', Hindi leaves it to the feminine verb forms. etāsām hetubhiḥ may be read 'by the reasons of these' with bala-abale as a separate object; the rendering takes 'strength and weakness of these (the sciences)' as the last object, with ca joining it to the three pairs. artha-anartha = gain and loss (glossary 9.7 reading; 'wealth' for artha belongs to dharma-artha). naya-anaya follows naya = policy; anaya could be read as 'misfortune' (aya/anaya of 6.2) but is paired here with naya. vyasana = calamity, the opposite of abhyudaya. avasthāpayati is literally 'causes to stand', often rendered 'keeps steady'. vākya = speech/utterance; prajñā = insight; vaiśāradya = proficiency. Long unit; medium confidence on the construction.",
